---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import BenchChart from '../components/BenchChart.astro';
import bench from '../data/bench.json';

const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
const pct = (n: number, base: number) => {
  const d = Math.round((n / base - 1) * 100);
  return d === 0 ? '±0%' : d > 0 ? `+${d}%` : `−${-d}%`;
};
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'results', text: 'Results' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'method', text: 'Method' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'limits', text: 'Limits' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'reproduce', text: 'Reproduce' },
];
---
<Prose title="Benchmarks" description="Token counts for JSON, TOON and LWON on six realistic datasets, with method and limits." headings={headings}>
  <h1>Benchmarks</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    How many tokens the same data costs as JSON, TOON and LWON. Every LWON result is decoded again and
    checked against the original before it is counted.
  </p>
  <div class="wide"><BenchChart /></div>

  <h2 id="results">Results</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table">
      <caption class="visually-hidden">Tokens per format and dataset</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Dataset</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">JSON indented</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">JSON minified</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">TOON</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">LWON</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">LWON vs JSON</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">LWON vs TOON</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {bench.results.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><span class="ds">{r.name}</span><span class="muted">{r.shape}</span></th>
            <td class="num">{fmt(r.tokens.pretty)}</td>
            <td class="num">{fmt(r.tokens.min)}</td>
            <td class="num">{fmt(r.tokens.toon)}</td>
            <td class="num"><strong>{fmt(r.tokens.lwon)}</strong></td>
            <td class="num">{pct(r.tokens.lwon, r.tokens.min)}</td>
            <td class="num">{pct(r.tokens.lwon, r.tokens.toon)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    LWON is smaller than minified JSON on every dataset. It is far ahead of TOON on nested, nullable
    and recursive data, slightly ahead on flat tables, and level on the search result, where long
    free-text snippets dominate and no format can compress prose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="method">Method</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Datasets are generated from a fixed seed so every run is identical. You can load each one in the <a href="/playground">playground</a>.</li>
    <li>Tokens are counted with the {bench.tokenizer} tokenizer.</li>
    <li>The baseline is minified JSON. Indented JSON is shown for reference only; comparing against it would overstate the savings.</li>
    <li>TOON output uses {bench.toon} with default options.</li>
    <li>LWON output uses the reference encoder with default options.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>o200k is one tokenizer. Claude and Gemini tokenize differently; their counts are being added.</li>
    <li>The datasets are synthetic, shaped after common API and tool payloads.</li>
    <li>Token count is not comprehension. Accuracy tests with real models are in progress, see <a href="/ai#accuracy">For AI</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="reproduce">Reproduce</h2>
  <pre class="code"><code>git clone https://github.com/ahmetzencirli/lwon
cd lwon
npm install
npm run bench</code></pre>
</Prose>

<style>
  .wide { margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  .ds { display: block; font-weight: 600; }
  th[scope='row'] .muted { font-weight: 400; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .table th[scope='row'] { background: none; font-size: 0.92rem; min-width: 12em; }
  .table-wrap :global(table) { border: 0; display: table; }
</style>
